INT. DECOMMISSIONED SUBMARINE, CORPORATE RETREAT - DAY

A cramped steel corridor. Pipes. Condensation. A banner: SYNERGY AT DEPTH.

BRANDEN, 40s, a regional director in a fleece vest, holds a clipboard. KIMBERLEIGH, 30s, in a pastel blazer, adjusts her lanyard. DEVONTE, 20s, an intern, hugs a thermos. PRUNELLA, 50s, finance, stares at a pressure gauge. GUNNAR, 60s, the museum guide, leans against a torpedo tube.

BRANDEN
Team! Gather round!

Nobody moves. There's nowhere to gather.

KIMBERLEIGH
Branden, there are five of us.

BRANDEN
Five is a team.

DEVONTE
Is that gauge supposed to be on red?

PRUNELLA
It's a museum. Nothing is supposed to be anything.

GUNNAR
That gauge hasn't worked since 1974.

BRANDEN
Great. Ice-breaker. Everybody say one word that describes our Q3.

KIMBERLEIGH
Dynamic.

DEVONTE
Damp.

PRUNELLA
Overdue.

GUNNAR
Submerged.

BRANDEN
Beautiful. Mine is "Lean."

PRUNELLA
Of course it is.

BRANDEN
Next: trust fall.

DEVONTE
Where?

BRANDEN
Backwards. Off the ladder.

GUNNAR
Please don't.

KIMBERLEIGH
Branden, I'd rather do the spreadsheet.

BRANDEN
That's the spirit!

He climbs the ladder. Turns. Falls. The others do not move. A very loud clang echoes through the sub.

BRANDEN (CONT'D)
(from the floor)
Okay. That's on me.
